{
  "dom_id": "step-q116315",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "The intensity $I$ of light, measured in $\\text{lux},$ is inversely proportional to the **square** of the distance $d,$ measured in meters, between the light source and the object being illuminated. A device that measures the light intensity is $12$ meters away from the light source and registers $4$ $\\text{lux}.$  What equation gives the relationship between $I$ and $d?$",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
